course: dictionary
lesson: 9418
title: Squid: arms, tentacles and ink
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A squid is a sea animal with a long, soft body. It has eight arms and two longer tentacles, so ten limbs in all. The tentacles have suckers only on their wide tips.
explain: When danger comes, a squid can squirt ink to escape. The ink makes a dark cloud that hides it. Squids also swim fast by squirting water out of their bodies.
explain: Squids are molluscs with no backbone, related to octopuses and snails. People also eat squid, especially fried rings called calamari.
fact: A squid is a sea animal with a long soft body, eight arms and two longer tentacles.
fact: Squid ink is a dark liquid a squid squirts to escape from danger.
fact: A squid has 3 hearts, like an octopus.
fact: The giant squid is one of the largest animals in the sea.
fact: Squids are molluscs with no backbone, related to octopuses and snails.
exercise: How many arms does a squid have? | Two | Six | *Eight | Ten
exercise: «A squid or cuttlefish has eight arms plus two longer tentacles.» How many limbs does it have in all? | Two | *Ten | Eight | Twelve
exercise: What does a squid squirt to hide from danger? | Water to make a loud noise | Sand to dig in | *Ink to make a dark cloud | Glue to stick to rocks
test: In «Narwhals dive to hunt halibut, squid and shrimps», what is a squid? | *Something a narwhal eats | A cold current | A kind of whale | A sea plant
test: «Giant squid were first filmed alive only in 2004.» What does this tell us? | People have filmed giant squid every year since 1900 | Giant squid were made in 2004 | *People had not filmed a live giant squid until 2004 | Giant squid have lived for 2004 years
exam: How many limbs and how many hearts does a squid have? | *Ten limbs and three hearts | Eight limbs and three hearts | Eight limbs and two hearts | Ten limbs and two hearts
